-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components and data

The proprietary license above applies ONLY to the Original Work. The components
below remain the property of their respective authors under their own terms.
Nothing is loaded from a network at runtime: every component is bundled as a
sibling file or inline, so the app runs fully offline.

  • three.js and OrbitControls (r136 / v0.136.0): MIT License,
    © 2010-2022 three.js authors, https://threejs.org. Vendored INLINE in
    index.html; the MIT license notice is retained at the embed.

  • Positions (`bodies.js`, `moons.js`, `probes.js`): derived from the JPL
    Horizons system, Solar System Dynamics Group, Jet Propulsion Laboratory,
    California Institute of Technology, https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/.
    Small-body radii and masses: JPL Small-Body Database,
    https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/tools/sbdb_lookup.html. Credit: NASA/JPL-Caltech.

  • HYG Database, version 3, by David Nash / astronexus: Creative Commons
    Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0),
    https://github.com/astronexus/HYG-Database. The file `sky.js` is a
    filtered, reformatted subset of this database (directions, magnitudes,
    and colors of the naked-eye stars) and is therefore itself licensed under
    CC BY-SA 4.0. It is NOT covered by the proprietary terms above.

  • Mission events for the rebuilt probes (`probes-rebuilt.js`): NASA Space
    Science Data Coordinated Archive (NSSDCA) and NASA mission pages, cited
    in `probe-events.md`.

  • Spacecraft launch dates: CelesTrak satellite catalog (SATCAT),
    https://celestrak.org.

  • Radii of Haumea, Makemake, Eris, and Arrokoth: the published papers cited
    in `tools/catalog.py`.

  • Saturn ring radii: NASA Saturnian Rings Fact Sheet (NSSDCA).
    Saturn pole orientation: IAU Working Group on Cartographic Coordinates
    and Rotational Elements, 2015 report.

